# Hilbert 90 for the absolute Galois group (the units of the algebraic closure)

For a field `k` with algebraic closure `k̄`, every *continuous* (equivalently, locally constant,
the coefficient module carrying the discrete topology) crossed homomorphism

`f : Gal(k̄/k) → k̄ˣ`,   `f (σ * τ) = f σ * σ (f τ)`

is a coboundary: there is `b : k̄ˣ` with `f σ = σ b / b` for all `σ`.  Equivalently,
`H¹(Gal(k̄/k), k̄ˣ) = 0`.

## Proof

`f` is locally constant, so `f⁻¹{1}` is an open neighbourhood of `1` (and `f 1 = 1` by the
cocycle identity).  The Krull topology is generated by the fixing subgroups of *finite normal*
subextensions, so there is a finite normal `M/k`, `M ⊆ k̄`, with `Gal(k̄/M) ⊆ f⁻¹{1}`; hence `f`
is trivial on `N = Gal(k̄/M)`.

* `f` is right-`N`-invariant (`f (a * n) = f a` for `n ∈ N`), since `f (a * n) = f a * a (f n)`.
* Consequently the values of `f` lie in `M`: for `n ∈ N`, `n (f a) = f (n * a) = f a`, using
  the normality of `N` and its right invariance.
* Choosing a lift `lift χ ∈ Gal(k̄/k)` of each `χ ∈ Gal(M/k)` we may descend `f` to a crossed
  homomorphism `g χ = f (lift χ) : Gal(M/k) → Mˣ` (well defined because of the right invariance
  on `N`), and finite Hilbert 90 (`Work.AbsoluteKummer.exists_algEquiv_div_of_isCrossedHom`)
  produces `b : Mˣ` with `g χ = χ b / b`.
* For arbitrary `σ`, `f σ = f (lift χ)` with `χ = σ|_M` (they differ by an element of `N`), and
  `σ` and `lift χ` act in the same way on `b ∈ M`; hence `f σ = σ b / b`.

## Main statement

* `Work.AbsoluteKummer.Hilbert90.exists_div_of_isCrossedHom`
-/
